WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.360
While most spider and scorpion bites cause only mild reactions like some redness and swelling,

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:10.480
certain venomous ones, like the black widow or brown recluse, can make someone very ill.

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:15.680
Small children and those with existing medical issues are at a higher risk for more severe

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:21.680
complications, so you'll want to keep a close eye on them. As you assess the person, watch for signs

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:26.879
like muscle cramps, fever, a headache, or more serious issues like difficulty breathing or

00:00:26.879 --> 00:00:32.240
fainting. If you notice severe symptoms like trouble breathing, intense pain, or an altered

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:38.560
mental status, call 911 immediately. For most situations, your immediate care is to wash the

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:44.400
wound with soap and water and apply an ice pack to manage the discomfort. For children, it is always

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:49.040
a good idea to follow up by calling poison control or their healthcare provider for further guidance.

00:00:49.599 --> 00:00:55.279
Finally, if you can do so safely and without touching the insect, try to take a photo of it.

00:00:55.279 --> 00:00:58.880
This can be incredibly helpful for medical professionals to identify

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:02.720
exactly what caused the bite and determine the best treatment.

